QuintoAndar downstream patch: batch DatasetAlias expansion while serializing a DAG.
Verified against Apache Airflow 2.11.2 in Astro Runtime 13.8.0.

To regenerate, copy the two installed Airflow modules from
/usr/local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/airflow, edit the copies, and produce:
  diff -u airflow/datasets/__init__.py{.orig,}
  diff -u airflow/serialization/serialized_objects.py{.orig,}
Normalize the paths to a/airflow/... and b/airflow/... so Dockerfile can apply
the result from the site-packages directory with `patch -p1`.

Caveat: the module-global cache is process-local and spans code under
@internal_api_call. It is valid for this Airflow 2.11 direct-database runtime,
but must be removed or redesigned before enabling AIP-44 internal API mode.

--- a/airflow/datasets/__init__.py
+++ b/airflow/datasets/__init__.py
@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@
 
